    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d459">

                <pb facs="0625" n="519" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg519"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Phelps to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-10-21"><hi rendition="#italic">October 21, 1891</hi>.</date>
                        (Received November 7.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 344.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose a copy of the last note I
                    addressed to the foreign office in regard to the case of John Haberacker.</p>
                <p>You will notice that as far as possible I made my protest against the unfavorable
                    decision of the case communicated to me on March 2 last entirely in the spirit
                    and almost in the words of Mr. Wharton’s instruction No. 229, of March 26. I
                    could not conceive a better form in which to present our argument.</p>
                <p>As yet I have received no answer.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. Walter
                    Phelps</hi>.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d459-a1.xml" xpointer="d459-a1"/>
            </div>
